/* Beat 5, composed onto ScreenScaffold and brought to `Splice Chamber
 * .dc.html` in Phase 9 Task 16.
 *
 * WHAT THIS SHEET IS FOR, STATED AS A TEST RATHER THAN AS A SIZE. Every
 * declaration below has to be something no component and no Theme class
 * provides: a geometry the handoff gives THIS screen and not the component
 * in general, an arrangement of components in a row or a column, or an
 * override the component's own comment says a screen is expected to make.
 * Anything that restates `.chip`, `.panel-*`, `.t-*`, `.elev-*` or a
 * component's internals belongs in the layer that already has it. The file
 * GREW in this task, and that is the right direction: it is now composing
 * seven components where it used to style two containers, and the handoff
 * gives this screen four geometries (74, 112, 40, 22) that are its own.
 *
 * WHAT LEFT IN PHASE 8 TASK 10 AND STILL HAS NOT COME BACK: the root's
 * gutter (the scaffold's content region), the three panel fills and inks
 * (`.panel-coral`/`.panel-amber` and `.t-danger`/`.t-warn`), the forecast
 * card's own surface and radius (`SectionCard`), and the CTA's whole
 * treatment (`.btn-primary`, through `CostCtaRow`).
 *
 * WHAT LEFT IN THIS TASK: `.splice-chamber-view__mutation`'s wrap and margin
 * are `MutationBanner`'s, which also owns the collapse; `.forecast-row`'s
 * row direction is `InheritanceBar`'s own; and the CTA's top margin is the
 * cost row's.
 *
 * AND WHAT LEFT IN TASK 16b: two GAPS this sheet was paying a second time.
 * The forecast column's `margin-top` and its `> .forecast-row` rule (the
 * bars' own 9px, restated) and the lineage strip's `margin-top` (the
 * track's own 8px, restated) are gone; each removal's own note, further
 * down, has what it double-counted and the handoff line it missed by.
 */
.splice-chamber-view { flex-grow: 1; }

/* ------------------------------------------------------------- the pair */

/* `Splice Chamber.dc.html:49` - `display: flex; align-items: stretch; gap:
 * 8px`. `align-items` defaults to stretch in UI Toolkit too, so the two
 * tiles are the same height whichever name is longer, which is what makes
 * them read as one control rather than two cards. The `gap` is on the
 * joiner's own margins below, because USS on 6000.6.0f1 has none. */
.splice-chamber-view__parents {
    flex-direction: row;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
}

/* BOTH HALVES OF THE STRETCH, AND `SectionCard.uss` SAYS WHY IN FULL.
 * `.section-card` IS the `.elev-1` wrapper: stretched by the row above and
 * left alone, the wrapper would take the taller tile's height while the
 * white surface kept its own, and the nine-slice would draw its drop around
 * bare paper below the shorter one. That is the defect that cost Task 14b a
 * capture, arrived at sideways - from a row rather than from a column. The
 * surface grows too, from here, which is the fix that note prescribes. */
.splice-chamber-view__parents > .splice-chamber-view__parent {
    flex-grow: 1;
    flex-shrink: 1;
    flex-basis: 0;
    /* TWO CLASSES FOR THIS ONE DECLARATION. `.section-card` carries
     * `margin-bottom: var(--space-2)` at the same single-class specificity,
     * and its sheet is attached deeper than this one - so a one-class rule
     * here would lose and the 8px would stay. It does no harm in a row, and
     * that is exactly why it would never have been noticed. */
    margin-bottom: 0;
}
.splice-chamber-view__parent > .section-card__surface {
    flex-grow: 1;
    /* The handoff's `border-radius: 18px; padding: 11px 12px 12px` at `:50`.
     * A literal rather than a token because 18 is not on the radius scale -
     * --radius-tile is 11 and --radius-card is 20 - and this project's rule
     * for one-off geometry is a literal beside the measurement it came from
     * (Tokens.uss's "Component geometry" block states it). The padding is
     * 12 on three sides against 11/12/12, one pixel over at the top. */
    border-radius: 18px;
    padding: var(--space-3);
}

/* A Founder the player already named is visibly out of reach, not hidden -
 * bible 3.3's rule read from the splice side. Unchanged from Phase 8 except
 * that the element it lands on is a `SectionCard` now. */
.splice-chamber-view__parent.locked-out { opacity: 0.4; }

/* `Splice Chamber.dc.html:55` - `justify-content: center; padding: 7px 0 6px`
 * around the creature. The slot itself is `HeroSlot`; this is the row that
 * centres it. */
.splice-chamber-view__parent-slot {
    align-items: center;
    margin-top: 7px;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
}

/* 64px, WHICH IS THE HANDOFF'S DRAWN ORNAMENT AND NOT ITS RESERVED BOX.
 * `:56` is a 74x74 svg on a `viewBox="0 0 100 100"`, and inside it the
 * dashed ring is `r 42` and the tinted disc `r 34` - so at the 0.74 scale
 * that box implies, the ring is 63.6px across and the disc 50.3. `HeroSlot`
 * draws its ring at the element's full edge (hero-ring.png fills its box)
 * and its disc at 80 of 96, so sizing the SLOT to the handoff's 74 would put
 * a 74px ring where the handoff has a 63.6px one - 16% heavier - and a 61px
 * disc against 50. Sized to the ornament instead, both land within a pixel.
 * The 10px of reserved box that goes missing is centring space in a row that
 * is already centred.
 *
 * THE DISC IS RESIZED WITH IT, AND IT HAS TO BE. `--hero-slot` is 96 and
 * `.hero-slot__disc` is a flat 80/40 in the component's own sheet, so a slot
 * shrunk on its own would have its disc overflow the ring. `HeroBand.uss`
 * makes the same three-rule move in the other direction for its haloed
 * subject, and for the same reason: a component's sheet reaches its own
 * descendants, and a screen's sheet reaches downward into the components it
 * composed. 25px is half of 50. */
.splice-chamber-view__parent-slot > .hero-slot {
    width: 64px;
    height: 64px;
}
.splice-chamber-view__parent-slot > .hero-slot > .hero-slot__disc {
    width: 50px;
    height: 50px;
    border-radius: 25px;
}

/* `:64` - 17px Baloo over `:65`'s 10.5px muted line, 1px apart. Ours is
 * `.t-section`'s --text-section (19px) in Baloo, 2 over the handoff's number
 * in the handoff's own face - `SpliceChamberView.ParentTile` has why that
 * beats `.t-card-title`'s 13px Nunito. The 1px gap is the handoff's own
 * `margin-top`. */
.splice-chamber-view__parent-name { white-space: normal; }
.splice-chamber-view__parent-role { margin-top: 1px; white-space: normal; }

/* `:66` - `flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 4px; margin-top: 8px`. Two chips on a
 * ~155px tile wrap on the longer trait names, which is what the handoff's
 * own `flex-wrap` is there for. */
.splice-chamber-view__parent-traits {
    flex-direction: row;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
}
/* VERTICAL ONLY, AND THE HORIZONTAL GAP IS DELIBERATELY NOT RESTATED.
 * `TraitChip` already owns the handoff's `gap: 4px` as 2px of margin on each
 * of its own sides - its sheet says so beside those two declarations. Adding
 * 4 more on the right made each chip 6px wider than it measures, and the two
 * chips on a 151px tile came to 154: they wrapped to a second row, 39px
 * tall, on both parents, for six pixels of restated spacing. Found in the
 * capture, not in a gate. */
.splice-chamber-view__parent-traits > .trait-chip { margin-bottom: var(--space-1); }

/* `:72-76` - a 40px column holding a 40px white disc with an 18px violet
 * glyph in it. `flex: none` so the two tiles divide what is left.
 *
 * 20px IS HALF OF 40, so this is a true circle: a square element clamps both
 * axes to the same number, which is the one shape immune to the lens defect
 * Theme.uss's header item 4 measured.
 *
 * THE 8px ON EACH SIDE IS THE ROW'S `gap: 8px` FROM `:49`, put on this child
 * because USS here has no `gap` - the same substitution every row in this
 * project makes. */
.splice-chamber-view__join {
    width: 40px;
    height: 40px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    align-self: center;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    border-radius: 20px;
    background-color: var(--surface);
    margin-left: var(--space-2);
    margin-right: var(--space-2);
}

/* The handoff strokes this mark `#7a6ac0` at 18px, which is --violet
 * exactly. It is a Label carrying U+00D7 rather than a tinted PNG -
 * `SpliceScreen.JoinMark` has the capture that decided it - so the size is a
 * font-size and the colour is a colour.
 *
 * 18px IS A LITERAL AND NOT A TYPE-SCALE STEP, deliberately: this is a
 * GLYPH at a drawn size, the same way `.cost-cta-row__icon` is 13px and the
 * pill's sparkle is 12px. Putting it on --text-section would tie an
 * ornament to the type ladder. */
.splice-chamber-view .splice-chamber-view__join-glyph {
    font-size: 18px;
    color: var(--violet);
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
}

/* -------------------------------------------------- the predicted hybrid */

/* THE BAND IS `HeroBand` AND THIS IS THE ONE PROPERTY IT CANNOT DEFAULT.
 * `--radius-band` is 26 and serves two of the handoff's six instances;
 * `Splice Chamber.dc.html:101` is 22, and `HeroBand.uss`'s own note says the
 * four screens that want something else override `.hero-band__surface` from
 * their own sheet - "that is expected, not a hack". This is that override.
 *
 * `overflow: hidden` IS LEFT ON ALTHOUGH THIS IS THE ONE HANDOFF INSTANCE
 * WITHOUT IT. The component sets it so a 264px ring cannot draw its dashes
 * outside a shorter band's corners; this band has `ring: false`, so there is
 * nothing to clip and the property is inert. Turning it off would be a
 * declaration whose only effect is to be different from the other five. */
.splice-chamber-view__predicted > .hero-band__surface {
    border-radius: 22px;
    /* `:101` - `padding: 13px 16px 14px`. --space-3/--space-4 are 12 and 16,
     * so the sides are exact and the top and bottom are a pixel and two
     * inside the handoff's. */
    padding-top: var(--space-3);
    padding-bottom: var(--space-3);
    padding-left: var(--space-4);
    padding-right: var(--space-4);
}

/* `HeroBand.uss` centres its subject because four of its six instances put
 * one thing in the middle of a band. This is one of the two that stack a
 * padded column instead, and that file names this screen as the case: "the
 * two that stack a padded column (Splice Chamber:101, Hybrid Growth:48)
 * override `align-items` and `justify-content` from their own sheet, which
 * is the direction a screen's sheet is allowed to reach." */
.splice-chamber-view__predicted .hero-band__subject {
    align-items: stretch;
    justify-content: flex-start;
    flex-grow: 0;
}

/* `:106` - `display: flex; gap: 13px; align-items: center; margin-top: 10px`. */
.splice-chamber-view__predicted-body {
    flex-direction: row;
    align-items: center;
    margin-top: 10px;
}

/* `:107` - a 112px square holding the ring, the pool and the art. THE
 * HANDOFF'S OWN NUMBER AT 1:1: this project's content column is 406px at the
 * 430 capture frame, which is the handoff's own frame, so nothing is scaled.
 * (`--hero-slot`'s 96px is the SAME measurement taken at a 390 frame in an
 * older task; `Tokens.uss` records that and 96 stays correct where a slot is
 * a list element.)
 *
 * THE DISC IS THE POOL AT `:110` - `r 46`, so 92px across, which is 82% of
 * the ring exactly as `HeroSlot`'s own 80-of-96 is 83%. The ring itself is
 * `r 54` (108px) against this element's 112, and the 4px is the ring's own
 * stroke and antialiasing margin in the svg. 46 is half of 92. */
.splice-chamber-view__predicted-slot { flex-shrink: 0; margin-right: 13px; }
.splice-chamber-view__predicted-slot > .hero-slot { width: 112px; height: 112px; }
.splice-chamber-view__predicted-slot > .hero-slot > .hero-slot__disc {
    width: 92px;
    height: 92px;
    border-radius: 46px;
}

/* `:116` - `flex: 1; min-width: 0`. The min-width has no UI Toolkit
 * equivalent and needs none: a flex child here shrinks below its content
 * width by default, which is the behaviour that declaration exists to
 * restore in CSS. */
.splice-chamber-view__predicted-text { flex-grow: 1; flex-shrink: 1; flex-basis: 0; }

/* `:117` - 22px Baloo. Ours is `.t-hero`'s --text-hero (28px), the nearest
 * thing on the scale and 6 over; `--text-card-hero` (26) is nearer but is
 * Task 14b's founder-card heading and borrowing it here would make one
 * screen's measurement into two screens' token. Named in the report as a
 * residual rather than forked here. */
.splice-chamber-view__predicted-name { white-space: normal; }

/* `:118` - 10.5px muted, 2px under the name. */
.splice-chamber-view__predicted-lineage { margin-top: 2px; white-space: normal; }

/* ---------------------------------------------------- the two card heads */

/* The handoff's two-sided card header - an uppercase eyebrow on the left and
 * a muted note on the right (`:102`, `:134`, `:184`). `SectionCard`'s own
 * heading is one 19px Baloo line and cannot be both, which is why these
 * cards are built without one; `SpliceChamberView.CardHeader` has the note.
 *
 * `align-items: center` RATHER THAN THE HANDOFF'S `baseline`, which UI
 * Toolkit does not have - it is silently dropped, like `text-transform` and
 * `calc()`. At 9px against 10px the difference is under a pixel. */
.splice-chamber-view__card-header {
    flex-direction: row;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: center;
}

/* The chip host inside a header, so a GenChip sits at the row's right edge
 * rather than stretching to the row's height. */
.splice-chamber-view__gen { flex-direction: row; }

/* `:136` and `:186` - 10px, 700, --mute, and NOT a `.lbl`: these two are
 * lowercase in the handoff and the eyebrow beside them is not. `.t-secondary`
 * is 11px in --mute, one over. */
.splice-chamber-view__note { flex-shrink: 0; }

/* ------------------------------------------------------- the two columns */

/* `:139` onward - the bars stack. A column rather than the Phase 8 row of
 * `StatCell`s: the handoff's rows are full-width and compared vertically,
 * which is what the bar inside each one is for.
 *
 * NO `margin-top` HERE, AND THE RULE THAT USED TO SIT UNDER THIS ONE IS
 * GONE - Phase 9 Task 16b. The pair read `margin-top: 10px` on this column
 * plus `margin-top: 9px` on `> .forecast-row`, and the second was a verbatim
 * restatement of `InheritanceBar.uss`'s own `.inheritance-bar { margin-top:
 * 9px }`. Identical value, so deleting it changes nothing - BUT the comment
 * beside it claimed "none above the first, which the container's own 10px
 * already provides", and that was wrong in a way the capture shows: the
 * first bar was taking the container's 10 PLUS the component's 9 = 19,
 * against `:139`'s 10. With this column's margin at 0 the component pays
 * every gap, first one included: 9 where the handoff draws 10 (one under,
 * on the component's own rhythm) and 9 between the rest, which is `:151`
 * and `:163` exactly. */
.splice-chamber-view__forecast { flex-direction: column; }

/* The empty case is one element in a column of rows, and unlike the Phase 8
 * row version it needs no `flex-grow` to fill the line - a column child
 * stretches across by default. The rule is kept as a NO-OP REMOVED rather
 * than carried forward: `.splice-chamber-view__forecast > .empty-state
 * { flex-grow: 1 }` would have grown the message vertically instead, which
 * is not what the old rule did in a row and not what this card wants. */

/* `:188` - the rail sits 8px under its header, AND `LineageStrip` ALREADY
 * PAYS IT. The rule that used to be here added --space-2 to `.lineage-strip`
 * on top of `LineageStrip.uss:29`'s own --space-2 on `.lineage-strip__track`,
 * so the rail sat 16px under the header against the handoff's 8 - Phase 9
 * Task 16b removed it. The sentence that justified it ("no component can own
 * this gap, because neither element is the other's descendant") was the part
 * that was wrong: the strip's FIRST CHILD is the track, the strip itself has
 * no padding, and UI Toolkit has no margin collapsing, so the track's own
 * top margin IS the gap under whatever sits above the strip. Kept as a
 * comment rather than a rule because the next screen to place a
 * `LineageStrip` under a header will reach for the same 8px twice. */

/* Two sentences, not labels, so they wrap. The coverage warning also
 * COLLAPSES when the server named nothing - SpliceChamberView.Bind has the
 * measurement. The mutation line is `MutationBanner`'s now and carries its
 * own wrap, its own margin and its own collapse. */
.splice-chamber-view__coverage-warning { white-space: normal; margin-top: var(--space-2); }
.splice-chamber-view__destruction-notice { white-space: normal; margin-top: var(--space-3); }
